# Advantages of Arrays

* Easy to store multiple values.
* Fast access using indexes.
* Simple to traverse.
* Efficient memory usage for sequential data.
* Useful for implementing many other data structures.

---

# Disadvantages of Arrays

* In many programming languages, arrays have a fixed size.
* Inserting or deleting elements in the middle can be expensive.
* Searching in an unsorted array may require checking every element.

> **Note:** Python lists are dynamic, so they can grow or shrink automatically. This is different from traditional arrays in languages like C.

